# The `update_xml` preflight writes <board>.xml at the project root on every
# KiBot run, purely as an intermediate the same run reads back (sheet-title
# lookups for the ToC). It's not a real deliverable — never commit it.
/*.xml

# RemoteLibrary/ (KiCad's local cache of parts placed from Prism's Remote
# Symbols panel) is intentionally NOT ignored here, see README.md section
# 2.4 and 7. Prism's own Release Studio build flags a missing footprint
# entry in fp-lib-table as a warning, meaning a clean checkout is expected
# to have these files present, not regenerate them on demand. Committing
# them keeps a fresh clone self-contained. See that section for the other
# half of this: sym-lib-table/fp-lib-table must use ${KIPRJMOD}-relative
# URIs, not absolute host paths, or committing this folder doesn't help.

# Generated outputs are committed back to the repo by CI (see ci.yaml) so
# README.md's embedded images and the fabrication/assembly documents are
# visible directly on GitHub, not just as a downloadable workflow artifact.
# Nothing in Schematic/, Manufacturing/, Testing/, 3D/, Images/, Reports/ is
# gitignored — those folders don't exist in a fresh clone until CI runs once.
